%U A400907 100285753889864145,3314178781908104384,116143926158711481697,4302211441168556076744,167957667648245792467171
%N A400907 Number of labeled loopless digraphs on n vertices such that deg^+(v) + deg^-(v) = 2 for every vertex v.
%C A400907 Here deg^+(v) and deg^-(v) denote the outdegree and indegree of v, respectively.
%H A400907 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A400907/b400907.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..404</a>
%F A400907 E.g.f.: exp(-x - x^2/2)/sqrt(1 - 2*x).
%e A400907 For n = 2, the only digraph has the arcs 1 -> 2 and 2 -> 1, so a(2) = 1.
%e A400907 For n = 3, each of the three edges of the triangle can be oriented in either direction, so a(3) = 2^3 = 8.
%e A400907 For n = 4, there are 3 labeled cycles of length 4, each with 2^4 orientations, and 3 ways to partition the vertices into two pairs, each joined by oppositely directed arcs. Thus a(4) = 3*2^4 + 3 = 51.
%Y A400907 Cf. A000165 (connected case, shifted by one for n >= 3).
%K A400907 nonn
%O A400907 0,4
